course: dictionary
lesson: 560
title: Audio: words about sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Audio means sound, especially sound that has been recorded or broadcast. In «audio guides» in museums, the recordings explain things as you walk round, so you listen instead of reading. When you meet a word like this, ask yourself: what is the sound part here?
explain: As an adjective, audio tells you the thing is to do with sound. In «an audio book», a voice reads the story to you. In «audio equipment», the machines are for recording or playing sound.
explain: Use the words around audio to check its meaning. Swap in "sound" and see if the sentence still makes sense: "audio guides" becomes "sound guides", which fits the museum idea. That is a good check.
fact: Audio means sound, especially recorded or broadcast sound.
fact: As an adjective, audio means to do with sound, as in «audio equipment».
fact: In computing, audio is the sound part of a video or a file.
fact: In Latin, «audio» means "I hear", as the sentences show.
fact: An audio guide is a recording that explains things as you walk round a museum.
exercise: «The museum's audio guide told us about the old coins as we walked round.» What is an audio guide? | *A recording that explains things as you walk round | A map printed on paper | A person who sells postcards | A ticket for the café
exercise: In «In Latin "audio" means "I hear"», what does audio mean in Latin? | I run | I go out | I see | *I hear
exercise: Which phrase means something to do with sound? | a red ball | *an audio file | a tall tree | a dark cave
test: In «audio cassette tapes», what does audio mean? | A shade of blue | *Recorded sound | Very old | Written text
test: In computing, what is the audio part of a video? | The subtitles | A picture | *The sound | The title
exam: Which meaning of audio fits «an audio guide» best? | A small machine that cooks food | Something you can only see | A type of paint | *Recorded sound that explains things
